Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 13:50:40 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 25/25] Modeling Algorithms - Close a fillet ending exactly in
 the plane of the face at its end

PerformCapOnEndFace closes a fillet with a cap on the face beyond the arc
where one of its sides leaves the support, when the trace of the fillet on
the opposite support face reaches that face: the end of the trace at the
vertex and its middle must lie on the two sides of it. When the fillet ends
exactly in the plane of that face, the end of the trace is on the plane, and
the sign of its distance is rounding noise. In the model of FreeCAD issue
32231 (a rim revolved over a quarter turn on a ring, the concave edges
between the outside of the ring and the end walls of the rim ending in the
top of the ring) the distance was +4e-17 at one end wall and -0 at the
other. One corner was capped in the top of the ring, the other went to
PerformIntersectionAtEnd, whose patch went up the rim to 2.7 above the top
of the ring for a radius of 0.2, with a tolerance of 0.012. A chamfer of
the same edges failed at both walls.

An end within the tolerance of the vertex now counts as reaching the face,
whatever the sign of its distance. The two corners are then alike: the
fillet or chamfer stops in the top of the ring and nothing above it
changes, which is what the FreeCAD pull request 32296 obtains by cutting
the result with a half space after the fact.

Test bugs/modalg_8/fillet_rim_on_ring_stops_at_ring_top, from the model of
the issue (data file freecad32231_rim_on_ring.brep); GTest for the same
construction, which does not hit the rounding but checks the result.

